    <!-- SECTION 06: CUSTOMER FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS -->
    <section class="section section-alt" style="padding: 2.75rem 0 2.25rem;" id="on-grid-faq">
      <div class="container" style="max-width:920px;">
        <div class="section-header animate-fade-up" style="text-align:center; margin-bottom:2rem;">
          <span class="section-tag section-tag-gold">Clear Answers</span>
          <h2 class="section-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
          <p style="color:var(--text-muted); font-size:1.05rem;">
            Everything you need to know about On-Grid Solar, net-metering, and government subsidies in Gujarat.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="sfh-faq-container">
          <div class="sfh-faq-item active">
            <button class="sfh-faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="true" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('active')">
              <span>01. What happens to my on-grid solar system during a power grid outage?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon">âˆ’</span>
            </button>
            <div class="sfh-faq-answer" style="display:block;">
              Under international safety standards (IEC 62116) and GERC grid codes, on-grid inverters feature mandatory <strong>Anti-Islanding Protection</strong>. If the municipal power grid goes down, the on-grid inverter immediately shuts down power export within milliseconds. This prevents electricity from flowing into street utility poles and protects DISCOM lineworkers from lethal electrocution while carrying out repairs.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="sfh-faq-item">
            <button class="sfh-faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('active')">
              <span>02. How do I get paid or credited for surplus solar units in Gujarat?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="sfh-faq-answer">
              Your utility installs a bi-directional smart net-meter that tracks both <em>Import</em> (units you pull from the grid) and <em>Export</em> (solar units you feed into the grid). Every month, your exported units are subtracted 1:1 from your consumed units. If you produce more than you consume, surplus units are banked with your DISCOM (Torrent Power, DGVCL, etc.) and carried forward. At the annual settlement, surplus credits are purchased at the GERC-notified APPC rate!
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="sfh-faq-item">
            <button class="sfh-faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('active')">
              <span>03. How much rooftop terrace space is required for a 3 kW or 5 kW on-grid setup?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="sfh-faq-answer">
              As a standard rule of thumb, you need approximately <strong>100 square feet of shadow-free rooftop terrace per 1 kWp of solar capacity</strong>. A 3 kW home system requires ~300 sq.ft, while a 5 kW setup requires ~500 sq.ft. With VOLT'S LEGACY's custom elevated pergolas (10ft clearance), 100% of your terrace floor remains completely open and usable beneath the solar panels for walking, gardening, and family gatherings!
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="sfh-faq-item">
            <button class="sfh-faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('active')">
              <span>04. Who handles the DISCOM approvals and PM Surya Ghar subsidy application?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="sfh-faq-answer">
              <strong>VOLT'S LEGACY manages 100% of the administrative paperwork on your behalf!</strong> We register your connection on the National PM Surya Ghar Portal, submit feasibility applications to Torrent Power / GUVNL, arrange Chief Electrical Inspector (CEI) testing, coordinate meter installation, and ensure your â‚¹78,000 subsidy is credited directly to your bank account via DBT.
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="sfh-faq-item">
            <button class="sfh-faq-question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('active')">
              <span>05. What is the expected lifespan and warranty of on-grid components?</span>
              <span class="faq-icon">+</span>
            </button>
            <div class="sfh-faq-answer">
              We install Tier-1 DCR-compliant N-Type TOPCon bifacial modules backed by a <strong>30-Year Linear Performance Warranty</strong> (guaranteeing over 80% output even at Year 30). Inverters carry 8 to 10-year manufacturer warranties, while our hot-dip galvanized mounting structures carry a 25-year structural corrosion warranty.
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
